## 5. TECHNICAL STACK & ENGINEERING STANDARDS

This is a frontend redesign integrated into an existing Astro 6 + Cloudflare Workers repo (dlocmot/dinamo-web). You must strictly respect the edge-runtime constraints:

*   *Astro Component Architecture:* Astro ships zero JS by default. All GSAP/Three.js logic must live inside client-side <script> tags or properly hydrated client islands (client:visible).
*   *Edge Runtime Safety:* NEVER import GSAP or Three.js in component frontmatter or SSR scope. It will break the Cloudflare Worker build. Keep the worker bundle lean; load Three.js dynamically via client-side import().
*   *View Transitions Lifecycle:* Ensure GSAP ScrollTriggers and Three.js renderers/geometries are correctly re-initialized on astro:page-load and completely disposed of on astro:before-swap to prevent memory leaks and double-binding.
*   *Backend & Content Integrity:* Preserve all existing CRM endpoints, magic-link auth, and Cloudflare bindings (D1/R2/Resend). Do not break server functionality. Keep all real contact data (RUC, address, emails) and legal disclosures fully intact.

